IMPORT prelude

-- Parity fixture for the built-in IMPLIES and NOT (UNKNOWN-EVALUATION-SPEC §8
-- step 2): jl4-mlir lowers IMPLIES with a short circuit, as it does AND and
-- OR, and its trace shows each connective with a child for each operand it
-- evaluated. Each function's cases are its truth table; the ones with a FALSE
-- left operand to IMPLIES never need the right one.
--
-- The NOT functions pin the trace of a negation: `NOT p` shares its source
-- range with `p`, and `NOT (p AND q)` with `p AND q`, so each needs a key of
-- its own in the trace's range map (jl4-mlir's 'exprDisambiguator').
--
-- `member implies paid` takes the facts as its own inputs, and its trace is
-- byte-identical to jl4-service's. `membership implies payment` reads them as
-- section GIVENs: its result matches, but its trace does not, because the
-- service reports a rule that reads only section GIVENs as one node, with no
-- children, whatever its body is.

§ `Membership dues`
    GIVEN `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
          `has paid` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Whether being a member implies having paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `membership implies payment` IS
    `is a member` IMPLIES `has paid`

@export The same implication, with the facts as the rule's own inputs
GIVEN member IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `member implies paid` IS
    member IMPLIES paid

@export Negation of an input
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not p` IS NOT p

@export Negation of a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not both` IS NOT (p AND q)

@export Double negation
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not not p` IS NOT (NOT p)

@export UNLESS, which is AND NOT
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `p unless q` IS p UNLESS q
